# Scan a topic's backlog (e.g. a dead-letter queue) and acknowledge every message once you've looked
# at it - the "scanning topics and acknowledge about consuming" priority from the brief.
#
# This seeds three throwaway messages first so the scenario is runnable standalone; against a real
# queue you'd usually skip the "produce" steps and just scan+acknowledge what's already there.

Scenario: Drain and acknowledge the dead-letter queue
Given use connection "local"
When produce message to topic "orders-dlq" value "poison message 1"
And produce message to topic "orders-dlq" value "poison message 2"
And produce message to topic "orders-dlq" value "poison message 3"
Then scan topic "orders-dlq" from beginning limit 50
And log message
# "log message" reports the most recently scanned message; all scanned messages get acknowledged below
# regardless of what was last logged.
And acknowledge each scanned message
